09:20:33.827356 IP 10.0.0.250.4569 > 84.16.64.240.4569: UDP, length: 12
09:20:33.827450 IP 10.0.0.250.4569 > 84.16.64.240.4569: UDP, length: 25

here is the full ruleset of NAT table at router1. Most of it are not relevant. 
However there are two types of UDP packets generated by asterisk: SIP (5060) 
and IAX2 (4569). Now, the SIP packets are routed correctly - they hit the 
SNAT rule and leave the router1 with source 192.168.100.1 but the IAX packets 
somehow manage to 'bypass' the iptables rules and leave unmodified...

irongate:~# iptables -t nat -nL
